---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { base } from "../lib/site";
---
<Layout
  title="Come to IU"
  description="Things you can do as an Indiana University Bloomington student: Welcome Week, student organisations, Little 500, IUDM, Sample Gates, and ordinary campus days."
  canonical="https://zhao-langxi.github.io/zhao-langxi/iu.html"
  current="iu"
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
      <p>Indiana University Bloomington · student life</p>
      <h1>Come to IU</h1>
      <p>
        A big campus with a small-community feel, if you actually walk out of your room.
        Official IU language calls it finding your people. I call it becoming someone who has a Tuesday ritual.
      </p>
      <p>
        What follows is a mix: things I have done, and things campus officially offers.
        I do not pretend I have joined all 900 organisations.
      </p>
    </header>
    <article>
      <section aria-labelledby="first-year-heading">
        <h2 id="first-year-heading">First year, if you are coming</h2>
        <p>
          Hoosier Welcome is weeks of meet-ups, CultureFest, and school events before you know where the
          good vending machines are. IU's
          <a href="https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/traditions.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">campus traditions page</a>
          is the official list. The unofficial one is: walk through
          <a href="https://bloomington.iu.edu/about/history.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sample Gates</a>
          until the limestone stops being a postcard.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started in Teter Hall. Striped carpet. Elevator doors. Room 102. Welcome Week, new names in the
          group chat, rush energy in the air even if you are only people-watching. Meeting someone on your
          floor who becomes your 2am study buddy and your Sunday brunch person. Fake flowers on the desk
          because real ones die and you are trying to make the room yours. A jade plant on the windowsill
          because your mum would want you to keep something alive.
        </p>
        <p>
          If some days you are homesick, that is allowed. Go home for a weekend. Let your people fuss.
          The boat photos are not the opposite of Bloomington. They are how you know what home feels like
          while you build a new one.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="people-heading">
        <h2 id="people-heading">Find people on purpose</h2>
        <ul class="direction-list">
          <li>
            <h3>beINvolved · 900+ organisations</h3>
            <p>
              IU lists more than 900 student organisations. Search them on
              <a href="https://beinvolved.bloomington.iu.edu/" rel="noopener noreferrer">beINvolved</a>.
              Try a first meeting. Walk out if it is not yours. That is self-discovery, not a scoreboard.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Student Involvement Fair</h3>
            <p>
              Held at Fine Arts Plaza / Showalter Fountain. Hundreds of tables, food trucks, and a chance
              to take a flyer without committing your whole semester. The 2026 fair was 27 August,
              4pm to 7pm.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Cultural centres and mentorship</h3>
            <p>
              Asian Culture Center, other cultural and identity centres, living-learning communities,
              and peer networks. Official map:
              <a href="https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/community/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Build your Hoosier circle</a>.
              I staff FASE MAP (Mentoring and Academic Planning) hours because I was the
              first-generation and low-income student asking those questions once.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Greek life, from the sidelines</h3>
            <p>
              More than 8,000 students are in sorority and fraternity life. You can cheer for friends,
              people-watch rush, and still know it is not the only way to find your people.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="traditions-heading">
        <h2 id="traditions-heading">Traditions that actually move campus</h2>
        <ul class="direction-list">
          <li>
            <h3>Little 500</h3>
            <p>
              Student bicycle race since 1951. A week of energy, then the races at Bill Armstrong Stadium.
              Spring 2026 was 24 to 25 April. Next up: 23 to 24 April 2027. The weekend has a personality.
              Bikes, crowds, that specific IU spring electricity.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>IU Dance Marathon (IUDM)</h3>
            <p>
              One of IU's biggest philanthropy weekends. Sleep deprivation, dancing, remembering this campus
              is larger than your to-do list. Official framing lives on the
              <a href="https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/traditions.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">traditions page</a>.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Homecoming and game day</h3>
            <p>
              Parade, football, cream and crimson. Memorial Stadium in the fall. Basketball at Simon Skjodt
              Assembly Hall ... Visit Bloomington still tells you to sing Sweet Caroline when the pep band
              plays it. Rec Sports, intramurals, and club sports if you want to play, not only watch:
              <a href="https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/athletics-recreation/" rel="noopener noreferrer">athletics and recreation</a>.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>The fight song</h3>
            <p>
              Written by a student in 1912. You will hear it until you know it. That is the point.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="everyday-heading">
        <h2 id="everyday-heading">Ordinary days that count</h2>
        <ul class="direction-list">
          <li>
            <h3>Sample Gates and the Old Crescent</h3>
            <p>
              Dedicated in 1987. Indiana limestone. The most-photographed IU structure. Walk through, then
              keep walking into Dunn's Woods ... twenty acres of beech and maple between the gates and
              Swain Hall.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Indiana Memorial Union (IMU)</h3>
            <p>
              Student hub. Free movies, the South Lounge leather chairs, Union Board events.
              <a href="https://imu.indiana.edu/about/index.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">IMU</a>
              is the official door.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Herman B Wells Library</h3>
            <p>
              Everyone claims a favourite floor. Find yours before finals week turns you into a ghost.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Eskenazi Museum of Art</h3>
            <p>
              Free. I have sat there with a clipboard that just said RELAX &amp; REFLECT. Visit Bloomington
              also tells students to lie back against the building at night and watch the light totem change
              colours. Do the museum first. The totem is extra.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>IU Cinema, Musical Arts Center, Auditorium</h3>
            <p>
              Film, Jacobs School of Music concerts, touring shows. You do not have to be a music major
              to sit in the dark and let something good happen.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>ServeIT, if you want work that leaves the gradebook</h3>
            <p>
              IU Luddy's nonprofit tech clinic. Students ship real sites for community partners.
              My first client was the City of Bloomington. That is one path. It is not the only one.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="official-heading">
        <h2 id="official-heading">Official starting points</h2>
        <ul class="proof-list">
          <li><a href="https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Campus life at IU Bloomington</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://beinvolved.bloomington.iu.edu/" rel="noopener noreferrer">beINvolved</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/events/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Upcoming student events</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.visitbloomington.com/blog/stories/post/40-things-every-iu-student-should-do-before-graduation/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit Bloomington · IU bucket list</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <a href={`${base}indiana.html`}>Indiana, beyond the gates</a>
          <a href={`${base}`}>Home</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
